{"diagnosis": "Trace shows TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero with tohost FAIL 0xdead. mem_la_addr drives low bits as 2'b10 instead of expected 2'b00, so every fetch is misaligned. Root cause is picorv32.v:382 which builds {next_pc[31:2]+mem_la_firstword_xfer,2'b10} and {reg_op1[31:2],2'b10}.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead) with no TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero"}

